---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How often should solar panels be cleaned in coastal NSW?',
    answer:
      'For properties within 2km of the coast across Sydney, the Central Coast, and Newcastle, panels should be optimized every six months. Airborne marine salt spray creates an invisible, alkaline crust that rapidly dulls output. For properties further inland, an annual optimization schedule is sufficient unless the array sits directly under heavy tree canopies, bird flight paths, or industrial soot corridors. Rather than relying on a calendar, monitor your inverter app; if your daily peak generation has dropped by 10% or more on a clear day compared to last season, your system is leaking money and requires optimization.',
    open: true,
  },
  {
    question: 'Why is robotic solar panel cleaning safer than traditional manual cleaning?',
    answer:
      'Traditional cleaning relies on operators walking across your roof matrix while wielding heavy, awkward extension squeegees. This creates an immense liability risk for property owners and frequently cracks fragile roof tiles, leading to costly internal water leaks. Salt Spray Solar eliminates this risk by deploying lightweight robotic solar crawlers. These automated machines distribute their under-7kg weight perfectly across your array using soft rubber tracks. They apply uniform, calibrated pressure without a single human footstep ever touching your solar frames or roof tiles.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can high-pressure washing be used to clean solar panels?',
    answer:
      'Absolutely not. Utilizing a high-pressure washer on solar infrastructure is a critical mistake that will void your manufacturer’s warranty. The intense pressure easily forces water past the factory rubber seals and straight into the sub-surface laminates, junction boxes, or internal wiring. This causes invisible, corrosive moisture damage that short-circuits the system months later. Abrasive household brooms and chemical detergents are just as destructive, as they strip away the anti-reflective glass coating engineered to maximize light absorption. We use exclusively soft, spinning nylon brushes and pure water.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why does the water quality matter for solar optimization?',
    answer:
      'Standard household tap water is full of dissolved minerals like calcium, magnesium, and iron. When sprayed onto hot solar glass under the Australian sun, the water evaporates instantly, leaving behind a cloudy, hard mineral scale. This white residue actively blocks sunlight and creates a rough texture that catches and traps future dust even faster. Salt Spray Solar utilizes a heavy-duty, 4-stage Reverse Osmosis and Deionization (RO/DI) filtration trolley on-site. We strip 100% of minerals from the water stream, delivering absolute 000-PPM pure water that dries completely crystalline and spot-free.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is a thermal imaging drone solar inspection, and do I need one?',
    answer:
      'Solar cell degradation and internal hardware faults happen silently beneath the glass and are completely invisible to the naked eye. Our premium aerial thermal imaging drone audits use infrared sensors to map the exact heat signatures of your system. When a cell has micro-fractures from storm damage, or when an internal bypass diode fails, it bottlenecks electricity and glows white-hot under infrared telemetry. We run these sweeps prior to cleaning to provide commercial facilities and residential clients with a clear digital health report, catching fire hazards and major component failures before they destroy your inverter setup.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Doesn’t standard rain clean my solar panels for free?',
    answer:
      'Only partially, and only on exceptionally steep roofs. On standard residential pitches or flat commercial warehouse roof lines, rain simply sheets across the glass, collects airborne dirt, and pools at the bottom edge frame. As it dries, it leaves behind a thick, opaque “grime band” directly over the bottom row of cells. Rain does absolutely nothing to dissolve baked-on bird droppings, tree sap, lichen, or sticky maritime salt films. In fact, rain frequently spreads coastal salt films evenly across the glass rather than lifting them off.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Will your solar optimization process void my manufacturer warranty?',
    answer:
      'No. Our process actively protects your investment. Major global solar panel manufacturers explicitly mandate the use of deionized, mineral-free water and soft-bristled brushes for routine maintenance. Furthermore, many premium panel brands require active, documented proof of regular professional maintenance to honor structural warranty claims if a component fails. Every robotic clean and thermal drone audit executed by Salt Spray Solar is digitally logged, providing you with a dated, compliant record for your manufacturer files.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to be home on the day of the service?',
    answer:
      'No, you do not need to alter your schedule. As long as our technical operator has clear, safe outdoor access to your property’s ground-level garden tap and a clear line of sight to the roof, we can complete the entire job independently. Once our robotic crawler and thermal drone sweeps are complete, we pack up, drain our buffer tank, and email your comprehensive digital efficiency and health report straight to your inbox.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is your pricing structure for a robotic optimization clean?',
    answer:
      'Because every roof line across the NSW corridor has a different panel configuration and height access profile, we maintain absolute pricing transparency via our online platform. Residential services feature a baseline call-out fee of $150 to $180 AUD which includes travel and your first 12 panels. Additional panels scale out at an affordable $8.00 to $15.00 AUD per panel. Commercial and industrial arrays are quoted on a custom sliding scale based on total volume and site compliance logistics. You can generate an instant, fixed price in under 60 seconds using our digital booking widget.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ — Salt Spray Solar"
  description="Answers on robotic solar panel cleaning, thermal drone inspections, pricing and warranty protection."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="FAQ"
    title="Clear Answers on"
    emphasis="High-Yield Solar Optimization"
    sub="Everything you need to know about professional robotic panel cleaning, infrared aerial diagnostics, and asset warranty protection across Sydney, the Central Coast, and Newcastle."
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions"><Button href={site.bookHref} variant="primary">Calculate My Instant Price &amp; Book Online</Button></Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <Section>
    <FaqList items={faqs} schema class="mt-0" />
  </Section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Still Have Questions About Recovering Your Lost Solar Output?"
    lede="Speak directly with the specialist technician who will be operating the machinery on your roof. Clear answers, high-tech execution, and guaranteed results."
    cards={[
      { label: 'Ready to Lock in Your Date?', tone: 'amber', href: site.bookHref, text: 'Calculate My Instant Price & Book Online' },
      { label: 'Need a Direct Call?', tone: 'teal', contact: true },
    ]}
  />
</BaseLayout>
